# A real BitLocker volume (AES-XTS-128), written by Windows BitLocker -- not built by this project.
# From the LEAPP cores' raw image fixtures, as carried in the comparison tool's tests/fixtures
# (2026.5.7), MIT -- fme/vendor/LICENSE-gleapp. Its key or passphrase was
# made for the fixture and opens nothing else.
#
# The expected answer, from how it was made: one BitLocker volume, locked; it opens with its startup key,
# bitlocker-xts128.BEK beside this file (made for the fixture; it opens nothing else), and holds a
# SquashFS file system -- tests/test_unlock.py.
# Without its key (this program does not ask for one) a run must say the
# volume is BitLocker-encrypted and locked, and that this is not an empty
# disk -- tests/test_real_encrypted_volumes.py.
